Python code for transferring money between two people (accounts) from one person to another. Code includes balance check and transfer test.
The initial and subsequent balances of the persons' accounts are also printed to demonstrate the successful transfer of money.
This program doesn't really show any transfer of money in a realistic way since the money is moved between a person and an imaginary account.
In a real-life scenario, a transfer between two accounts of two different people involves some form of money moving/transaction and there should also be a check if the sender has permission to transfer money, etc. But in this simplified model, we simply subtract from one person's account and add to another person's account. We also consider if the person has sufficient balance in his account for the transaction. If not, it will throw an error and the transaction will not happen. If everything goes well, our function will return a success message. 
If the error handling is not implemented correctly, it would potentially stop the entire program, and hence, we perform error handling at the function level. 
This is a simple case verification in which two instances/people/accounts were involved."""
